import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 492 | Cross-IP Synthesis: Five-Level Standard Overview of Protagonist-Uniqueness Dependency","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 492 | Cross-IP Synthesis: Five-Level Standard Overview of Protagonist-Uniqueness Dependency","no":492,"module":2,"tags":["Cross-IP Synthesis","Protagonist Uniqueness","Five-Level Standard","Tang Luo","Ye Fan","Gu Chensha","Heng Yuan Zhou"],"related":["17-Plane-Transcendent Strongest Standard","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","29-Symbiotic-Degree Assessment System"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0492_模块2-跨IP综合-主角唯一性依赖度五级标准总览.md","filePath":"en/0492_模块2-跨IP综合-主角唯一性依赖度五级标准总览.md"}'),o={name:"en/0492_模块2-跨IP综合-主角唯一性依赖度五级标准总览.md"};function a(r,e,l,d,h,u){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="entry-492-cross-ip-synthesis-five-level-standard-overview-of-protagonist-uniqueness-dependency" tabindex="-1">Entry 492 | Cross-IP Synthesis: Five-Level Standard Overview of Protagonist-Uniqueness Dependency <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-492-cross-ip-synthesis-five-level-standard-overview-of-protagonist-uniqueness-dependency" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 492 | Cross-IP Synthesis: Five-Level Standard Overview of Protagonist-Uniqueness Dependency&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Cross-IP Synthesis (Entry 1) | Benchmark base: Documents 17, 04, 29</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-one-ruler-measures-the-myriad-realms" tabindex="-1">Introduction: one ruler measures the myriad realms <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-one-ruler-measures-the-myriad-realms" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: one ruler measures the myriad realms&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Since Entry 251 introduced &quot;protagonist-uniqueness dependency,&quot; this library has used it to judge Tang Luo (252–287), Ye Fan / Shrouding the Heavens (288–301), Tang San / Douluo, Ji Ning / Desolation Era (406–431), Wukong / Dragon Ball (432–467), Zheng Zha / Infinite Terror (468–477), Jackie Chan / Jackie Chan Adventures (478–484), Gu Chensha / Dragon Rune (485–491). This entry formally standardizes this ruler into five levels, as the unified ruler for Module 2 entries 252–500. Heng Yuan Zhou (Myriad-Spirits Balanced-Anchor Origin Universe)&#39;s six top-level axioms — anti-predation axiom, republican axiom of Myriad Races, collective ascension axiom, causal self-discipline axiom, <strong>law-first axiom</strong>, universal equal infinite law as core — among which the collective ascension axiom directly corresponds to &quot;the lower the uniqueness dependency, the better.&quot; The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-cross-ip-summary" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Cross-IP Summary) <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-cross-ip-summary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Cross-IP Summary)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Energy waste positively correlates with uniqueness dependency: the higher the dependency, the more civilizational-grade energy concentrated on one person; the greater the waste. Gu Chensha (extremely high) waste greatest; Heng Yuan Zhou (extremely low) waste least.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-cross-ip-summary" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Cross-IP Summary) <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-cross-ip-summary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Cross-IP Summary)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Uniqueness dependency is civilizational fragility. Each level&#39;s regression mechanism:</p><ul><li><strong>Extremely high</strong>: protagonist falls, cosmos collapses (Gu Chensha)</li><li><strong>High</strong>: protagonist falls, civilization regresses hundreds of years (Tang Luo, Zheng Zha)</li><li><strong>Medium-high</strong>: protagonist falls, order chaos for decades (Jackie Chan)</li><li><strong>Medium</strong>: protagonist falls, oligarchic group takes over (Ye Fan)</li><li><strong>Extremely low</strong>: any individual absence does not affect (Heng Yuan Zhou)</li></ul><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-cross-ip-summary" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (Cross-IP Summary) <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking-cross-ip-summary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking (Cross-IP Summary)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory thinking positively correlates with uniqueness dependency: the higher the dependency, the more the protagonist tends to concentrate civilization&#39;s key functions on himself.</p><h2 id="iv-five-level-standard-overview-table" tabindex="-1">IV. Five-Level Standard Overview Table <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-five-level-standard-overview-table" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Five-Level Standard Overview Table&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Dependency</th><th>Civilizational Form</th><th>Representative IP/Protagonist</th><th>Key Feature</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Level 5 · Extremely High</td><td>Civilization survival tied to one person</td><td>Single-Log</td><td>Gu Chensha (Dragon Rune 485–491)</td><td>Myriad Ranks &quot;being-made-dragons&quot;; he carries everything for them</td></tr><tr><td>Level 4 · High</td><td>Protagonist present = order present</td><td>Gift-Style</td><td>Tang Luo (252–287), Zheng Zha (468–477)</td><td>Universal benefit tied to one person&#39;s goodwill; institutions absent</td></tr><tr><td>Level 3 · Medium-High</td><td>Strong-one group absent = turmoil</td><td>Gift-Style-Leaning-Oligarchic</td><td>Jackie Chan (478–484), Wukong (432–467)</td><td>Protagonist + small circle; civilization zero construction</td></tr><tr><td>Level 2 · Medium</td><td>Dependence on a few strong ones</td><td>Oligarchic</td><td>Ye Fan (288–301), Shi Hao, Ji Ning (406–431)</td><td>Ten-thousand years of peace surnamed X; institutions not established</td></tr><tr><td>Level 1 · Extremely Low</td><td>Order written into institutions and network</td><td>Network-Type</td><td>Heng Yuan Zhou</td><td>Anchor Council + Alaya + Myriad-Ranks republicanism</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan-cross-ip-method" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan (Cross-IP Method) <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan-cross-ip-method" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan (Cross-IP Method)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Quest Sediment Domain for each IP does a &quot;protagonist absence experiment&quot;: remove the protagonist from peak period, observe civilization collapse time. The five-level standard is reverse-derived from these collapse times: extremely high = collapse in 7 days; high = collapse in 10 years; medium-high = collapse in 100 years; medium = turmoil in 100 years; extremely low = no collapse.</p><p>This five-level standard&#39;s universality lies in: it does not depend on any specific IP&#39;s settings; only measures one structural parameter — <strong>civilization key functions&#39; distribution concentration.</strong> Gu Chensha concentration highest (four cosmos functions on one person), Tang Luo next (civilization-rebuilding function on one person), Ye Fan again (Great Emperor position on one family), Heng Yuan Zhou lowest (functions distributed across council + court + supervisory committee + Alaya Network). This parameter can be cross-IP compared, cross-era compared, cross-cosmos compared. It is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s &quot;thermometer&quot; for judging all civilizational forms — no need to ask protagonist good/evil, only measure this parameter, to know how long this civilization can live.</p><p>The five-level standard&#39;s practical use is giving every new IP quick positioning. Given a new IP, no need for per-entry decomposition; only ask three questions: first, how long after protagonist absence does civilization collapse? Second, how many people are civilization&#39;s key functions concentrated on? Third, is order written into institutions or into an individual? Three answers come out, five-level standard immediately positions. This standardized positioning makes Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s benchmark critique no longer &quot;each IP individually analyzed,&quot; but &quot;batch checkup, triage&quot; — five-level standard is the triage desk; six transformation modules are the treatment plan.</p><p>The five-level standard&#39;s other value is making &quot;critique&quot; operable. In the past, Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s critique on each IP was &quot;per-entry decomposition, per-entry qualitative assessment,&quot; time- and effort-consuming. With the five-level standard, new IP comes in, three questions can position; after positioning, directly invoke six transformation modules. <strong>Critique is no longer art, it is engineering.</strong> This is precisely Heng Yuan Zhou methodology&#39;s core: turn subjective judgment into objective parameters; turn personal taste into institutional standards. The five-level standard is this methodology&#39;s first result.</p><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Self-consistency law</strong>: the higher the uniqueness dependency, the lower the setting self-consistency (because &quot;protagonist always present&quot; itself is a setting)</li><li><strong>Retcon risk law</strong>: the higher the dependency, the higher the retcon risk (because protagonist must keep getting stronger to maintain uniqueness)</li><li><strong>Heng Yuan Zhou reference</strong>: the only cosmos reaching &quot;extremely low dependency + high self-consistency&quot;</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the higher the dependency, the more energy concentrated on one person</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: uniqueness = predation; bringing civilization&#39;s key functions back to one person</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo is level 4, higher than most predatory schools, still not level 1</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: only level 1 (network type) can truly cover Myriad Ranks</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: only level 1 can infinitely expand without collapse</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The protagonist-uniqueness dependency five-level standard is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s unified ruler for judging all Myriad-Realms IPs. It does not judge protagonist good/evil; it only judges structural stability. <strong>The greater the protagonist, the more dangerous — because the greater he is, the more Myriad Ranks do not need themselves.</strong> Module 2&#39;s remaining entries will use this ruler to measure predation typology, regression paths, ending forms.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./251_模块2-唐罗体系拆解-总论三重上限与主角唯一性评判.html">Entry 251 · Tang Luo Overview</a> · <a href="./485_模块2-龙符-总论古尘沙与独木式文明定性.html">Entry 485 · Dragon Rune Overview</a> · <a href="./500_模块2-模块二终章-诸天对标批判库总结-从掠夺到共生的文明跃迁.html">Entry 500 · Final Chapter</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',27)])])}const m=i(o,[["render",a]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
